[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="QuestResource" load_steps=6 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Quests/QuestResource.cs" id="1_quest"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Quests/ObjectiveResource.cs" id="2_obj"]

; Phase 41D - the first quest in the game with two paths, and the caller for both halves of the
; sub-phase: the branch gates (RequiredFlagId) and the ordering bool (SequentialObjectives).
;
; ⚠️ THE BRANCH IS CHOSEN BEFORE THE QUEST EXISTS, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE SAFETY OF IT. The flag is
; set by one dialogue choice and the quest is started by the choice on the NEXT node - the two-choices-
; deep shape the ledger run already uses in this same graph, because a DialogueChoice carries ONE
; effect. So there is never a frame where this quest is in the log with no path picked. That matters:
; a quest whose objectives are ALL gated has nothing live until a flag lands, and "all zero live
; objectives are met" is trivially true. QuestProgress refuses to complete on zero live objectives for
; exactly that reason - but relying on that guard instead of authoring around it would be building the
; content on top of the backstop.
;
; ⚠️ THE TWO FORK CHOICES GATE ON EACH OTHER (MissingFlag), NOT ON THE QUEST. A player can set a flag
; and walk off without starting the quest - the accept node is still one choice away - and on coming
; back the un-taken fork must be gone, or both flags end up set and BOTH paths run at once. Gating
; each fork on the other's absence closes that and, for free, gives the walked-off player their own
; path back to the accept node.
;
; ⚠️ SequentialObjectives IS THE POINT OF THE ORDER, AND THE ORDER READS ODDLY ON PURPOSE. The four
; objectives are declare-reach, declare-talk, hush-reach, hush-talk - so on the hushed path the first
; TWO objectives are inert, and objective 2 is live immediately because the sequential scan steps over
; earlier objectives whose gate is shut. Without that step-over an ordered branching quest would lock
; itself forever behind the path not taken. Interleaving the pairs would work identically; keeping each
; branch contiguous is what makes the .tres readable.
;
; ⚠️ NEITHER PATH PAYS DIFFERENTLY, AND THAT IS A DECISION (maintainer call). The ending is the FLAG,
; and the flag has live consumers that already existed: shop.hollowreach.hull opens a gated shelf on
; flag.hollowreach.barrels_hushed, and Sedge has a different line for each. Per-outcome reward tables
; were considered and declined - a second place rewards live is invariant 5 waiting to happen, and the
; consequence a player actually feels here is what the world does afterwards.
;
; ⚠️ NO PrerequisiteQuestId, FOR 41C's REASON. A gate only a human can open is a gate no instrument
; sees behind: with one on, --panelshots could not start this quest and neither branch would ever be
; photographed. quest.hollowreach.word is the natural lead-in and is deliberately NOT required.

